{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["And he prophesied concerning them: <b>Behold, a people rises like a lion</b> — this is the cub — and afterward it exalts itself like a lioness, and it does not lie down in its land until it eats prey and drinks the blood of the kings of Canaan, as Onkelos says (Onkelos on Numbers 23:24). Now in this second prophecy he added to tell Balak that they would conquer the land and slay mighty kings. Now Balak knows that Israel would not inherit his land, and therefore even though he has now told them that in the end they would defeat the kings of Canaan, he still wishes him to curse them by means of his enchantment so that he himself might prevail over them, or perhaps he might be able to wage war against them and strike some of them. Therefore he said further, \"And I will take you to another place; perhaps it will be upright in the eyes of HaElohim and He will curse them for me from there\" (Numbers 23:27). Not that he would reverse his blessing, for he had already informed him, \"El is not a man, that He should lie, nor a son of man, that He should relent\" (Numbers 23:19), but he reasoned: behold, they are destined to conquer the land of Canaan, which is their inheritance, and to slay its kings, but perhaps I shall prevail over them and strike them, as the Amalekite and the Canaanite dwelling in that mountain did, who struck them as far as Hormah (Numbers 14:45). And this is his intention, out of his fear of them, as he mentioned to the elders of Midian (Numbers 22:4). Or perhaps his purpose was that he might recover for him whatever Sihon had seized from the territory of Moab, as is explicit in the words of Jephthah, which I have already mentioned."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "אלהים (in the phrase עיני האלהים) rendered HaElohim per the voice rules; the name of God is not translated into English."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:18.774588690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}